    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75819" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐλάς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>, ἡ, pecul. fem. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὖλος</span> (B), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>crisped, crinkled</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαίτη
			δρυός</span>, of oak-leaves, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				260
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
				Subst., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πήρα, θύλακος, πτωχῶν οὐ.
					ἀεὶ κενεή</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				360
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυλὰς</span> cj. Ruhnken for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐλαὶ, κενεή</span> Hecker for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεναί</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> s. vv. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυλίδες, θυλλίς,
			οὐλάδες</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				1.53
			</span></i>; restd. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὖδας</span> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.413
			</span></i> (Antip.).</div>
